<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Naucratis</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Naukratis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Naucratis was a Greek trading city in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile-delta">Nile Delta</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, founded in the 7th century BCE. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">Pharaoh</a> Amasis in the 6th century it became the only port where Greek merchants were allowed to trade, and cities such as Miletus, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samo">Samos</a>, Aegina, Chios and Mytilene kept sanctuaries there, several of them sharing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hellenion">Hellenion</a>. It was a key channel for exchange between Egypt and the Greek world.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/naucratis.jpg" alt="Naucratis" width="320" height="304" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Plate_sphinx_BM_GR1965.9-30.705.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
